      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.21,
      "end_seconds": 5.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Hi there, the chair's free, sit down. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.56,
      "end_seconds": 14.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "I wanted to get burning pain in the upper tummy looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.71,
      "end_seconds": 19.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Alright, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.22,
      "end_seconds": 26.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Since last Tuesday, that's when it began"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.29,
      "end_seconds": 30.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Have you noticed any triggers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.87,
      "end_seconds": 35.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Yes, an empty stomach. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.77,
      "end_seconds": 39.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "have you been feeling full quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.49,
      "end_seconds": 44.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Yeah. Six months, um, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.56,
      "end_seconds": 47.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Any indigestion as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.85,
      "end_seconds": 49.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Yes, since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.54,
      "end_seconds": 67.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Did you get black stools or vomiting blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.79,
      "end_seconds": 73.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.89,
      "end_seconds": 78.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Have you had any weight loss or difficulty swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.97,
      "end_seconds": 82.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.77,
      "end_seconds": 87.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.94,
      "end_seconds": 90.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.92,
      "end_seconds": 95.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.99,
      "end_seconds": 98.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.8,
      "end_seconds": 102.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.75,
      "end_seconds": 107.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.31,
      "end_seconds": 110.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.38,
      "end_seconds": 116.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.18,
      "end_seconds": 121.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "So, are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.42,
      "end_seconds": 125.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.76,
      "end_seconds": 132.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.81,
      "end_seconds": 141.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "I'm on diclofenac, 50 milligrams, when needed. It's ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, three times a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.96,
      "end_seconds": 143.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Yes, carry on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.26,
      "end_seconds": 162.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.95,
      "end_seconds": 169.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Arthritis in my knees, for two years. I have high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.35,
      "end_seconds": 179.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.14,
      "text": "yes, carry on okay, I can see high cholesterol in your file as well okay, did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.89,
      "end_seconds": 185.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "I had a bunion operation six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.78,
      "end_seconds": 203.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.16,
      "end_seconds": 207.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 208.51,
      "end_seconds": 224.29,
      "duration_seconds": 15.78,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Height 177 centimetres, blood pressure 118 over 70, temperature is 36.8 degrees, saturation 98 percent, weight 78 kilos, BMI works out to 24.9, respiratory rate 18, heart rate 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.37,
      "end_seconds": 228.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "good, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.62,
      "end_seconds": 233.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.12,
      "end_seconds": 235.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "of course"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.88,
      "end_seconds": 239.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.34,
      "end_seconds": 256.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "your upper tummy is tender in the middle with no guarding"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.48,
      "end_seconds": 287.54,
      "duration_seconds": 28.06,
      "text": "right, please sit back down let me tell you where I've got to i'd lean towards a possible stomach ulcer from anti-inflammatory tablets. Reflux is also on my list i'll request a stool test for helicobacter, it'll help with dyspepsia i'll request a blood count, it'll help with dyspepsia i'm prescribing omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day, eight weeks you take it by mouth that should help with stomach ulcer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.57,
      "end_seconds": 308.23,
      "duration_seconds": 19.66,
      "text": "Stop the ibuprofen and and use paracetamol for the knee pain instead. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Let's plan a check in six weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.67,
      "end_seconds": 312.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
